  "metadata": {
    "title": "Dataset for Root Segmentation Beyond Species Boundaries: A Generalizable Framework for Anatomical Analysis",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17726414",
    "publication_date": "2025-11-26",
    "description": "<p><strong>Code available at <a href=\"https://github.com/janetkok/Root-Segmentation-Beyond-Species-Boundaries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://github.com/janetkok/Root-Segmentation-Beyond-Species-Boundaries</a><br>Dataset Overview</strong> This dataset provides annotated imagery for the semantic segmentation of Pearl Millet and Sorghum crops. It is designed to support both binary and multiclass segmentation machine learning tasks.</p>\n<p><strong>Repository Structure</strong> The dataset is organized into two main distinct directories:</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>binary/</strong>: Designed for binary segmentation models.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Content: Pearl Millet images.</li>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Annotations: Ground truth binary segmentation masks (Foreground/Background).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>multiclass/</strong>: Designed for multiclass segmentation models.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Content: Images of both Pearl Millet and Sorghum.</li>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Annotations: Ground truth multiclass segmentation masks.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Experimental Splits</strong> To ensure consistent evaluation, standard Training and Validation splits are provided for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; Pearl Millet only.</li>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; Sorghum only.</li>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; Combined Dataset (Pearl Millet + Sorghum).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Funding</strong><br>This work was supported by the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council (grant number BB/Y513908/1) and Agence National de la Recherche (SorDrought grant ANR-23-CE20-0052).</p>",
